1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
This is the implementation demo for journey thirteen.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,610
It is the real application and API running on this machine,

3
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:12,770
with synthetic people and the local adapters, so nothing is charged or sent.

4
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:16,850
It shows a buyer lining up the cars they have had inspected.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,580
This buyer has had four cars inspected in the same window.

6
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,920
They open Compare from the navigation.

7
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:28,240
Three cars have an estimate, so they are lined up lowest all-in first,

8
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:33,120
where all-in is the asking price plus the cost to get the car safety certified.

9
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,840
The cheapest is marked as the lowest all-in.

10
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,540
The fourth car is still waiting for its mechanic's estimate,

11
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:43,240
so it sits at the end and says so, rather than disappearing.

12
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:47,870
The note reminds the buyer that the cheapest car isn't always the best car.

13
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:52,010
Opening the lowest car's report shows the same total as its column.

14
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,820
The same page on a phone.

15
00:00:54,820 --> 00:01:00,260
The cars stack in one column, each with the same details: the car, its kilometres,

16
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:04,180
the all-in total, the asking price and the cost to certify.

17
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:09,490
The lowest all-in car keeps its mark, and the car still waiting for its estimate

18
00:01:09,490 --> 00:01:10,620
still comes last.

19
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:16,000
Nothing scrolls sideways, so a buyer can compare cars while standing next to one.

20
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:19,520
The rules are enforced by the server.

21
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:23,540
The buyer with four cars gets the four, with the lowest marked.

22
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,570
A different buyer, with two cars of their own, gets only those.

23
00:01:27,570 --> 00:01:30,960
A buyer with no inspections gets an empty comparison.

24
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:34,730
The mechanic is refused, and so is a request with no token.

25
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:39,200
The lowest car's own report shows the same all-in total as its column,

26
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:42,520
because the comparison is computed from the reports.

27
00:01:43,670 --> 00:01:45,490
Here is what to remember.

28
00:01:45,490 --> 00:01:50,060
Compare lines up the cars from one window, lowest all-in first.

29
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:54,050
A car without an estimate stays in the list as pending.

30
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:58,620
It works on a phone, and a buyer only ever sees their own cars.

31
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:02,240
Not built yet: the car's make, model and location.

32
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:05,870
Next, journey fourteen: review inspection history.
